Package: evtests
Title: Tests and Diagnostics for the Upper Tail of a Distribution
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Rodrigo Fonseca", "Villa", email = "rodrigo03.villa@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-2938-2270"))
Description: Semiparametric tools to examine the upper tail of a sample before
    an extreme value analysis: tests of the extreme value condition, tests of
    the domain of attraction and of a finite end-point, estimators of the
    extreme value index and of the end-point, and the choice of the number of
    upper order statistics. Includes the tests of Hasofer and Wang (1992)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.1992.10475189>, Segers and Teugels (2000)
    <doi:10.1023/A:1011411212045>, Dietrich, de Haan and Husler (2002)
    <doi:10.1023/A:1020934126695> with the critical values of Husler and Li
    (2006) <doi:10.1007/s10687-006-0025-8>, Neves, Picek and Fraga Alves
    (2006) <doi:10.1016/j.jspi.2004.09.008>, Drees, de Haan and Li (2006)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jspi.2005.02.017>, Neves and Fraga Alves (2007)
    <doi:10.1007/s11749-006-0010-1>, Neves and Pereira (2010)
    <doi:10.1016/j.spl.2009.11.021>, del Castillo, Daoudi and Lockhart (2014)
    <doi:10.1111/sjos.12037> and Fraga Alves, Neves and Rosario (2016)
    <arXiv:1412.3972>, the goodness-of-fit tests of Choulakian and Stephens
    (2001) <doi:10.1198/00401700152672573>, the end-point estimators of Hall
    and Wang (1999) <doi:10.2307/3318618> and Fraga Alves and Neves (2014)
    <doi:10.5705/ss.2013.183>, and the choice of the number of upper order
    statistics of Drees and Kaufmann (1998)
    <doi:10.1016/S0304-4149(98)00017-9>, Danielsson, de Haan, Peng and de
    Vries (2001) <doi:10.1006/jmva.2000.1903>, Guillou and Hall (2001)
    <doi:10.1111/1467-9868.00286> and Bader, Yan and Zhang (2018)
    <doi:10.1214/17-AOAS1092>. Each method is tested against the numerical
    results of its source paper, and the differences found are documented.
